  'A 217-foot railroad bridge of the Pegram truss type, made in 1894 by the Edge Moor Bridge Works of Wilmington, Delaware, and moved to the Big Wood River in 1914. It carried Union Pacific trains from 1936 to 1981, among them the ski trains to Sun Valley. The Blaine County recreation district made it a footbridge in 1984 and it joined the National Register in 1997 (Wikipedia).',
